Article 65: Expulsion from Public Transactions

Exclusion from public transactions entails banning from direct or indirect participating in all transactions or agreements proposed by:
1.	State;
2.	A territorial decentralized community;
3.	A public establishment;
4.	A State controlled or concession enterprise or enterprise controlled by a territorial decentralized community.

The penalty of exclusion may be either definitive or temporary for a duration of 5 (five) years at the most.

