Sub-Section 2 Reprimand

Article 76: Legitimacy of Reprimand

When the accused receives a jail sentence the maximum of which is less than or equal to 3 (three) years, the court can pronounce the reprimand if the following three conditions are met:
1.	disturb to the public order resulting from the offence has come to an end;
2.	damage was repaired;
3.	the offender shows his/her willingness for social reintegration.

