text:
CHAPTER 1 CRIMES OF GENOCIDE

Article 183: Acts of Genocide

Constitutes as crimes of genocide, each of the acts when committed with an intention of destroying, in whole or in part, a national, ethnic, racial or religious group described as follows:
1.	murder the members of the group;
2.	aggressive attack against physical or psychological integrity of the members of the group;
3.	submitting the members of the group to conditions that entail total or partial destruction of the group;
4.	setting up measures to impede the births within the group;
5.	forced transfer of the children of the group to another group.

