text:
Article 212: Aggravating Circumstances Depending on Targets

The crime described in 210 (Tortures and Barbarous Acts) is punishable by an imprisonment from between 10 (ten) to 20 (twenty) years when it is committed:
1.	on a victim or a civil party in order to prevent the latter from denouncing the offence or demanding the reparation of the damage;
2.	on the witness in order to prevent the latter from becoming a witness during an inquiry, an investigation or a court proceeding;
3.	on a victim or a civil party because he/she has denounced an offence or has demanded the reparation of his/her damage;
4.	on a witness due to his/her testimony given during an inquiry, an investigation or a court proceeding.

