SECTION 2 EXTORTION

Article 363: Extortion

Extortion is an act of obtaining, by violence, threat of violence or coercion:
1.	a signature;
2.	a commitment or a renunciation;
3.	a disclosure of a secret;
4.	a delivery of funds, of assets or of any property.

