Sub-Section 2 Accepting of Bribery

Article 594: Accepting Bribery

It is punishable by an imprisonment from 7 (seven) years to 15 (fifteen) years for any act committed by a civil servant or a citizen entrusted with public mandates through an election to directly or indirectly solicit or accept without authorization the donation, gift, promise, or any interest in order:
1.	to perform any act of his/her functions to facilitate anything using his/her functions;
2.	not to perform any act of his/her functions to facilitate anything using his/her functions;

