text:
Article 607: Intimidation

Sub-Section 3 Intimidation

It is punishable by an imprisonment from 2 (two) years to 5 (five) years and a fine from 4,000,000 (four million) Riels to 10,000,000 (ten million) Riels any intimidation against a civil servant or a citizen entrusted with public mandates through an election so that:
1.	the public servant or elected citizen performs any act of his/her function;
2.	the public servant or elected citizen not performs any act of his/her function;
3.	the public servant or elected citizen will abuses his/her real or assumed influence, in order to obtain an employment, a contract, a distinction or any other preferences.

